      "writtenOn": "2026-09-18T18:49:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "While in local testing adding the outsetBoundsForAA test helped the overlap issues you were seeing, I think we need to generalize this code to account for the fact that the end caps are being aligned out to the tile size. \n\nCurrently the !renderer check for path atlases works because it just so happens that the final CoverageMask shapes that are rendered are tight to the AA-outset pixel bounds. Unless the end caps clip their rendering to be tight to exclude all the rows/cols that are fully transparent, we actually want this to be rounded out to the tile granularity.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1711,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 1713,
        "endChar": 5
      },
      "revId": "c9056b49d9dc8fd0044c7e56770387dd57ef2c75",
