    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "182378e4_c7b2b21f",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/Device.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 27
      },
      "lineNbr": 2295,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-18T18:49:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think that a cleaner approach that will have other benefits for Graphite is to generalize the concept of the PathAtlas option to something like a GeometrySpawner(??) that takes in the original geometry and does additional upfront work to produce N actually recorded draws, with the option to change the Renderer in use and adjust the final bounds, and have the ability to flush when out of internal resources.\n\nPath atlases would convert to a CoverageMask and its associated renderer. We could hopefully fold text subruns into this system, and the strip generator otherwise is like a more advanced path atlas. It opens up the potential for other optimizations, such as applying a dash on a line and emitting a number of instances w/o having to repeat the overhead of the paint prep and clip walking, or allowing a drawn SkRegion to be split into a bunch of recorded rectangles. When drawListLayers is the universal way of doing things, I think it would also be interesting to see if we can eliminiate the extra layer/bounds checking for these multi-recordDraw() cases by finding the insertion layer based on the original full bounds and then inserting into that layer the multiple spawned subgeometries.  It could also generalize the inner-fill and the wide-cap tiles that don\u0027t have coverage to automatically adjust to the opaque paint ID and insert at the stop layer.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2295,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 2295,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "c9056b49d9dc8fd0044c7e56770387dd57ef2c75",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
